# Copy to .env and edit. Every line is optional; run.sh reads this file.

# The machines whose Claude Code sessions are shown, in the order of their blocks on
# the display (at most 6). The machine the hub runs on is read directly; the others
# over SSH as the user the hub runs as (key-based, no passphrase prompt), with the
# probe script piped over, so nothing needs installing there except `claude` itself.
# Default: just this machine.
#AGENT_CONTROL_HOSTS=devbox,laptop,buildbox

# Where the device key is read from (default ~/.config/agent-control/device_key),
# or the key itself.
#AGENT_CONTROL_DEVICE_KEY_FILE=~/.config/agent-control/device_key
#AGENT_CONTROL_DEVICE_KEY=

# Port and address the hub listens on.
#AGENT_CONTROL_PORT=8767
#AGENT_CONTROL_BIND=0.0.0.0

# The "+" button: open a new Claude Code session on this machine's desktop, using
# this .desktop launcher (its id: the file name without .desktop). Leave the host
# empty to switch the button off. On a GNOME desktop, the repository's
# desktop/install.sh writes agent-control-new there, whose terminal is raised and
# marked; elsewhere, examples/claude-terminal.desktop is a starting point.
#AGENT_CONTROL_NEW_SESSION_HOST=devbox
#AGENT_CONTROL_NEW_SESSION_LAUNCHER=agent-control-new

# Tapping a session: a shell command run on that session's machine to bring its
# terminal window to the front. {id} is replaced by the session id and {pid} by its
# process id; {state} by the row's state (working, waiting, done, ...) and {title} by
# its title, already shell-quoted into one word (use it bare, not in quotes of your
# own). It runs in a non-login shell, so give a full path; single quotes keep
# $HOME for that machine's shell to expand. Exit 0 = raised; otherwise a stderr line
# "agent-control: <reason>" is shown on the display.
# Unset: a tap only highlights the row. On a GNOME desktop, the repository's
# desktop/install.sh installs this one, which raises the window and marks it in the
# state's colour with its title (see desktop/README.md); on others, write your own.
#AGENT_CONTROL_FOCUS_COMMAND='$HOME/.local/bin/agent-control-window raise {pid} --highlight {state} {title}'

# The one-line "what's left for you to do" under each finished session is written
# by `claude -p --model haiku` on the hub's machine (your Claude plan, one short call
# per finished turn). Default: the claude CLI found on PATH or in ~/.local/bin.
# Set it empty to switch the lines off.
#AGENT_CONTROL_CLAUDE=

# Usage gauges: a Prometheus server holding claude_allowance_used_percent{window=...}
# and claude_usage_last_fetch_timestamp_seconds (see the README). Empty = no gauges.
#AGENT_CONTROL_PROMETHEUS=http://prometheus.local:9090
# Which allowance windows to show, in order, and their labels (at most 3 windows;
# a label is cut to 5 characters).
#AGENT_CONTROL_USAGE_WINDOWS=seven_day=WEEK,seven_day_fable=FABLE,five_hour=5H

# Seconds between probe reports from each machine.
#AGENT_CONTROL_INTERVAL=3
